<title>USA: Litton protests award to Avondale.</title>
<headline>Litton protests award to Avondale.</headline>
<dateline>WOODLAND HILLS, Calif 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Litton Industries said it filed a protest with the General Accounting Office of the Navy's LPD-17 contract award to Avondale Industries Inc.</p>
<p>The total value of the award with options was about $1.5 billion. The total program value was estimated at $7.0 billion.</p>
<p>&quot;We're protesting the award with the intent of having the Navy reverse its decision,&quot; said a Litton spokeswoman.</p>
<p>The Navy awarded the contract to Avondale on December 17 to build the LPD-17, an amphibious ship that would put troops ashore on helicopters and landing boats.</p>
